 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Keep a safe distance behind the car in front of you, at least twice its length. That way, if the driver stops suddenly, you have time to stop too. Try to keep a good gap anyway. Most people drive too close, and it makes the road busy and dangerous. Be alert at junctions, especially those with views blocked. Cars coming from behind can surprise you. It is, which is why we always stop and check both ways, and let pedestrians cross in front of us.",
